ing which investor categories meet the $200 million threshold, particularly for the January 1981 treasury bill issuance. The key is to identify which specific investor groups demonstrate substantial holdings in these specific maturity-date securities.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_b4e708676e9446d4","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1980_03.json | python3 -c \"\nimport json\nimport sys\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\n\n# Get the table with Jan 1981 data for Treasury bills - regular weekly and annual maturing\n# This is Table TSO-3\ntable = data['document']['elements'][910]['content']\n\n# Let's find the Jan. 1981 row \nimport re\n# Find all table rows\nrows = re.findall(r'<tr><td>([^<]+)</td><td>([^<]+)</td>(.*?)</tr>', table)\n\nfor row in rows:\n    issue = row[0]\n    if 'Jan. 1981' in issue:\n        print('Issue:', issue)\n        print('Total:', row[1])\n        # Get the remaining cells\n        cells = re.findall(r'<td>([^<]+)</td>', row[2])\n        print('Cells:', cells)\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
