ly 0) < $200M ✗\n- Insurance companies (fire, casualty, and marine): * (essentially 0) < $200M ✗\n- Savings and loan associations: 7 < $200M ✗\n- Corporations: 148 < $200M ✗\n- States and local governments (general funds): 76 < $200M ✗\n- States and local governments (pension and retirement funds): * (essentially 0) < $200M ✗\n\nI see that only two investor categories meet the criteria: U.S. Government accounts and Federal Reserve banks, and commercial banks. These are the only groups with holdings exceeding $200 million in January 1981.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_db1b6a6429cdd4c4","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1980_03.json | python3 -c \"\nimport json\nimport sys\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\n\n# Get the table \ntable = data['document']['elements'][910]['content']\n\n# Let's parse all the Treasury bills rows\nimport re\n# Find all table rows\nrows = re.findall(r'<tr><td>([^<]+)</td><td>([^<]+)</td>(.*?)</tr>', table)\n\n# Find the Jan. 1981 row for regular weekly and annual Treasury bills\nfor row in rows:\n    issue = row[0]\n    # Match only 'Jan. 1981' (not '9-3/4 Jan. 1981-P' which is a Note)\n    if issue.strip() == 'Jan. 1981':\n        print('Issue:', issue)\n        print('Total:', row[1])\n        # Get the remaining cells\n        cells = re.findall(r'<td>([^<]+)</td>', row[2])\n        print('Number of investor cells:', len(cells))\n        \n        # Define the investor categories - these are the 7 from the problem\n        investor_categories = [\n            'U.S. Government accounts and Federal Reserve banks',\n            'Commercial banks',\n            'Mutual savings banks',\n            'Insurance companies (life)',\n            'Insurance companies (fire, casualty, and marine)',\n            'Savings and loan associations',\n            'Corporations',\n            'State and local governments (general funds)',\n            'State and local governments (pension and retirement funds)'\n        ]\n        \n        print()\n        print('Holdings for each investor category for Jan. 1981 Treasury bills:')\n        print('-' * 70)\n        \n        # These are in order based on the header\n        # Note: the table also has 'all other investors' which is not one of the 7 categories\n        \n        # Let's see what's in cells\n        for i, cell in enumerate(cells):\n            # Clean up the value - remove commas\n            val = cell.replace(',', '')\n            if val == '*':\n                val = '0'\n            try:\n                val = int(val)\n            except:\n                val = 0\n            \n            if i < len(investor_categories):\n                status = '> $200M' if val > 200 else '<= $200M'\n                print(f'{investor_categories[i]}: {cell} ({status})')\n        \n        # Note: There's also 'all other investors' which is the last cell\n        print(f'All other investors: {cells[-1]}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
